---

## Applicability Note

This project is currently a **Prototype / POC** (Phase 1 — local deployment on user's machine). Per the steering document, the following are deferred:

- PrivateLink / VPC endpoints (no AWS infrastructure in Phase 1)
- AgentCore Identity (local stdio transport, ambient credentials acceptable)
- AgentCore Observability (basic stderr logging is sufficient)
- VPC Flow Logs, Config rules (no VPC in Phase 1)
- Automated prompt-validation test suites (no direct LLM invocation by this server)
- SigV4 for multi-agent calls (single-agent local mode)
- Tagging, centralized logging, change-set policies (no IaC deployment yet)

When this prototype moves to Phase 3 (AWS cloud deployment), all deferred items must be closed.

---

## ✅ Controls Satisfied

### Credentials & Secrets
- [x] No hardcoded credentials in source code
- [x] Credentials loaded from external config.json (file-permission restricted)
- [x] config.json is in .gitignore — never committed to version control
- [x] Refresh token used for short-lived access token acquisition via STS-like LWA flow
- [x] Token auto-refresh before expiry (5-minute buffer)
- [x] Credentials never logged to stdout/stderr
- [x] Credentials never returned in MCP tool responses (spapi_get_config is sanitized)
- [x] Error responses sanitized — only return error codes and request IDs, not raw API bodies

### Data Protection
- [x] TLS 1.2+ explicitly enforced via Node.js https.Agent (minVersion: "TLSv1.2")
- [x] All SP-API communication over HTTPS — no plaintext HTTP
- [x] PII gated behind Restricted Data Tokens (RDT) — not returned by default
- [x] Input validation via Zod schemas on all tool parameters before API invocation
- [x] Path parameter validators prevent traversal characters (../ \)

### Dependencies & Supply Chain
- [x] npm audit --omit=dev: 0 known vulnerabilities in production dependencies
- [x] Minimal dependency footprint (5 production dependencies)
- [x] Dependencies use semver ranges limited to minor/patch updates
- [x] No eval(), exec(), or dynamic code execution anywhere in codebase
- [x] No prototype pollution vectors (no unsanitized object spreading)

### Authentication
- [x] OAuth2 token refresh is race-condition safe (promise coalescing pattern)
- [x] Mock mode blocked when NODE_ENV=production
- [x] Access tokens stored only in memory — never written to disk

### Rate Limiting & Resilience
- [x] Per-API-domain rate limiting via Bottleneck (queue-before-fail)
- [x] Exponential backoff retry (3x) on transient errors (429, 5xx)
- [x] 30-second HTTP timeout prevents hanging connections
- [x] Auto-pagination capped at configurable max_total_results (default 1000)

### Access Control
- [x] Account-type filtering: vendor tools inaccessible in seller mode and vice versa
- [x] Tool lookup validates visibility before execution
- [x] Structured error with suggested action returned for unauthorized tool access

---

## ⚠️ Medium Priority — Close Before Production (Phase 3)

### M1: Credentials should move to AWS Secrets Manager
- **Control:** Credentials & Secrets — Use Secrets Manager or SSM Parameter Store
- **Current state:** Credentials stored in local config.json file
- **Gap:** Local file storage is acceptable for POC but not for multi-user/cloud deployment
- **Files to update:** `src/auth/aws-provider.ts` (to be created in Phase 3)
- **Fix:** Implement AWS Secrets Manager credential provider that reads per-tenant secrets

### M2: No CloudTrail / CloudWatch logging
- **Control:** Logging & Monitoring — Enable CloudTrail, CloudWatch alarms
- **Current state:** Logging is stderr-only via Pino (local consumption)
- **Gap:** No centralized, auditable log trail for API calls or auth events
- **Files to update:** `src/utils/logger.ts`, new `src/observability/` module
- **Fix:** Add CloudWatch Logs integration in Phase 3 ECS deployment; structured audit events for tool invocations

### M3: No Infrastructure as Code
- **Control:** IaC — Define all infrastructure in code
- **Current state:** Phase 1 has no AWS infrastructure (local only)
- **Gap:** Phase 3 deployment will need CDK/CloudFormation for ECS, API Gateway, Secrets Manager
- **Files to update:** New `infra/` directory with CDK stack
- **Fix:** Create CDK stack before Phase 3 deployment; scan with cfn-lint and checkov

---

## 📋 Low Priority — Production Hardening (Phase 3+)

### L1: VPC endpoints for AWS service access
- **Control:** Networking — Use VPC endpoints to avoid public internet
- **Current state:** Local deployment makes no AWS service calls (only SP-API over public HTTPS)
- **Gap:** Phase 3 ECS deployment should use VPC endpoints for Secrets Manager access
- **Deferred per:** POC applicability — PrivateLink optional for prototypes
- **Files to update:** `infra/vpc-stack.ts` (to be created)

### L2: Container security hardening
- **Control:** Containers — Non-root users, read-only filesystems, minimal base images
- **Current state:** No container (runs as local Node.js subprocess)
- **Gap:** Phase 3 ECS Fargate task definition should specify non-root user and read-only root FS
- **Deferred per:** POC applicability
- **Files to update:** `infra/task-definition.ts` (to be created)

### L3: Resource tagging
- **Control:** IaC — Tag all resources with owner, environment, cost-center
- **Current state:** No AWS resources to tag
- **Gap:** Phase 3 resources need consistent tagging
- **Deferred per:** POC applicability — tagging deferred for prototypes
- **Files to update:** `infra/` CDK constructs

### L4: Bedrock Guardrails (if AI integration added)
- **Control:** AI Workloads — Deploy Bedrock Guardrails on all invocations
- **Current state:** This server is a tool provider, not an LLM invoker. No direct Bedrock calls.
- **Gap:** If future phases add Bedrock for response formatting or summarization, guardrails needed
- **Deferred per:** Not applicable to current scope — server provides tools to an external AI agent
- **Note:** The AI agent (Amazon Quick) is responsible for its own guardrails; this server only returns raw SP-API data

### L5: Automated security scanning in CI/CD
- **Control:** Post-Build Security Review — generate/update security.todo
- **Current state:** Manual review (this file)
- **Gap:** No automated CI pipeline running npm audit, dependency checks, or static analysis
- **Files to update:** `.github/workflows/security.yml` or `buildspec.yml` (to be created)
- **Fix:** Add CI step that runs `npm audit`, `eslint --security-plugin`, and generates this file

